---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Gallery" description="See real Chudware modeling, manufacturing, and onboarding workspaces captured from the product.">
  <header class="page-hero gallery-hero"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Product gallery</p><h1>Actual product. No concept renders.</h1><p class="lede">Every image below comes from Chudware itself. They show the current interface and scenario-driven product states rather than composited marketing mockups.</p></div></header>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap gallery-grid">
      <figure class="gallery-card gallery-card-wide"><div class="gallery-media"><img src="/images/modeling.png" width="1340" height="838" alt="Chudware parametric modeling workspace showing an enclosure with Box, Fillet, and Shell features" /></div><figcaption><p class="eyebrow">Model</p><h2>Parametric enclosure</h2><p>A box, fillet, and shell remain visible as ordered features beside the model.</p></figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="gallery-card"><div class="gallery-media"><img src="/images/cam.png" width="1340" height="838" alt="Chudware manufacturing workspace showing a CAM job, stock, tools, operations, and simulation controls" /></div><figcaption><p class="eyebrow">Manufacture</p><h2>CAM workspace</h2><p>Stock, tools, operations, simulation, and post-processing controls stay with the design.</p></figcaption></figure>
      <figure class="gallery-card"><div class="gallery-media"><img src="/images/onboarding.png" width="1340" height="838" alt="Chudware onboarding screen for choosing a starting engineering workspace" /></div><figcaption><p class="eyebrow">Start</p><h2>Workspace onboarding</h2><p>Choose modeling, drawing, simulation, electronics, manufacturing, PLM, AI, reverse engineering, or another product workspace.</p></figcaption></figure>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
